 pair: obs_0152 versus obs_0149, same heading but shifted 0.75 m west, giving useful parallax on the structure edge. I'm examining the gray mass boundary in obs_0152, which runs diagonally toward roughly (270, 300), and want to back-project this using mask analysis.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Translation achieved with matched heading — obs_0149 and obs_0152 are both h=180, 0.75 m apart. That's the parallax baseline I needed."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UzbLktHEpHMSDejGNR4dcL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom PIL import Image; import numpy as np, math\nim=np.asarray(Image.open('observations/obs_0152.png').convert('RGB')).astype(int)\nR,G,B=im[:,:,0],im[:,:,1],im[:,:,2]\npx,py,h=2.200,7.400,180.0\nhr=math.radians(h); fw=(math.sin(hr),math.cos(hr)); rt=(math.cos(hr),-math.sin(hr))\ndef bp(u,v,z=0.0):\n    if v<=258: return None\n    D=(1.55-z)*256.0/(v-256.0); L=D*(u-256.0)/256.0\n    return (round(px+D*fw[0]+L*rt[0],3), round(py+D*fw[1]+L*rt[1],3), round(D,2))\n# tan floor\ntan=(R>140)&(R<210)&(B<G)&((R-B)>15)\nprint('TAN floor topmost (junction) / bottommost')\nfor u in range(150,512,20):\n    c=np.nonzero(tan[:,u])[0]\n    if len(c)<3: print(u,'none'); continue\n    print(u,'vt',c.min(),bp(u,c.min()),'vb',c.max(),bp(u,c.max()))\n\" 2>/dev/null"}}]},"8af5267db8a6c7ca93158d0f20257a074daf4a64da7f56de95adf8c48787734f":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool result metadata: {\"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_01P97qoZB4cXGVnTRgDvxjAv\", \"type\": \"tool_result\", \"is_error\": false}"},{"type":"text","text":"344,352,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-2.68, 1.57, 4.13)\n326,352,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-2.47, 1.36, 4.13)\n358,351,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-2.88, 1.71, 4.18)\n0,392,1.249,3.484,225 -> (1.25, -0.64, 2.92)\n64,375,1.249,3.484,225 -> (0.66, -0.64, 3.33)\n128,358,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-0.13, -0.64, 3.89)\n192,347,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-1.06, -0.37, 4.36)\n256,344,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-1.94, 0.3, 4.51)\n320,341,1.249,3.484,225 -> (-2.88, 1.01